{
    "background_story": "Shelby was a humble and unassuming artist who never sought to draw attention to herself. Despite her incredible talent, she consistently underquoted her prices, preferring to focus on the art rather than the profit. Her modesty often led people to underestimate her abilities, but those who commissioned her work were always blown away by the quality and detail she delivered. As her reputation grew, so did the demand for her art, but Shelby remained true to her values, never inflating her prices or seeking to capitalize on her success. Her understated nature belied a fierce dedication to her craft, and those who knew her admired her integrity and commitment to creating something truly beautiful.",
